<p>Seiichi Niikuni&#8217;s 1966 poem &#8220;River/Sandbank&#8221; consists entirely of the Japanese kanji characters for &#8220;river&#8221; (&#24029;) and &#8220;sandbank&#8221; (&#24030;), each repeated to fill an isosceles right triangle, so the resulting square illustrates its subject matter.</p>
